// MCST Elbrus (e2k) system call numbers, generated from the lcc delivery's
// asm/unistd.h (the e2k kernel table is its own i386-style remap, NOT the
// x86_64 one). Names the e2k kernel does not implement are pinned to -1L:
// the kernel routes an unknown number to sys_ni_syscall, so the call yields
// ENOSYS instead of reaching a wrong handler. pread64/pwrite64 map onto the
// table's pread/pwrite — identical ABI, historical naming.
//
// SPARK: regenerate after an lcc delivery update:
// values from <lcc>/fs/usr/include/asm/unistd.h, names from x86_64_sprt/syscall.h
